# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the nightly tsan_gcc14 run.
#
# The AWS C++ SDK (aws-sdk-cpp / aws-crt-cpp / aws-c-s3 / aws-c-common) runs
# its own event-loop threads and synchronises them with custom atomics and
# cross-thread reference counting that ThreadSanitizer does not understand. As
# a result it reports false data races when an S3 meta-request completes and is
# cleaned up on one SDK thread while another SDK thread is still finishing it
# (seen from StorageConcurrentReadBackMatchesDiskOnS3, which reads an S3
# storage from two threads). These are third-party SDK internals, not
# percona-binlog-server code; races in our own code are still reported, because
# the patterns below match only the SDK's own functions.
race:aws_s3_meta_request
race:aws_mutex_
race:aws_mem_
race:aws_ref_count
race:aws_atomic
race:Aws::Free
race:Aws::Malloc
